< xtContent="BASIC WORKFLOW",d=S(),p=c("p"),p.textContent="The core workflow for using NEBaseChanger i
< s:",v=S(),_=c("ul"),_.innerHTML=`<li>enter the target DNA sequence,</li>  	<li>define the range
<  of the mutation region,</li> 	<li>specify the mutation (deletion/insertion/substitution),</li>  
< 	<li>and view/save the results.</li>`,b=S(),w=c("p"),w.textContent='Specification of the muta
< tion target and action varies with the specific application mode: "AA Point Mutation", "Indel/Substi
< tution", "Batch", or "Legacy". Each mode is intended to add convenience for the task at hand, but mo
< st operations can be specified in any selected mode. AA Point mutation mode is most convenient if th
< e mutagenesis is limited to one or more single codons, whereas the general Indel/Substitution mode w
< orks with larger (and smaller) single insertions and substitutions and also allows deletions. Batch 
< mode is designed for a longer list of mutations and allows mixing of point and indel styles of entry
< .',y=S(),A=c("p"),A.textContent=`Legacy mode is intended to emulate NEBaseChanger V1 and produce res
< ults that are consistent with the parameters used in V1. Principally, the minimum primer length is r
< eset to 18 nt and insertions are always in the 5\u2032 tails.  Legacy mode has a simpler interface t
< hat will be	familiar to users of V1, but it is limited in functionality.`,q=S(),T=c("a"),T.textC
< ontent="\u2191 Back to top",N=S(),M=c("h3"),M.textContent="SEQUENCE ENTRY",k=S(),E=c("p"),E.textCont
< ent='Enter a DNA sequence by copying and pasting it into the sequence text area or uploading a file 
< from your computer. Acceptable formats for the DNA sequence are raw (plain text without IDs and desc
< riptions), FASTA (first line consisting of ">ID optional description"), or GenBank. For convenience,
<  a list of common vectors is provided, accessible from the dropdown menus above the sequence entry a
< rea.  Selecting the "Use Reverse Complement" checkbox instructs NEBaseChanger to use the reverse com
< plement of the sequence entered in the sequence text area. Selecting the "Partial" checkbox tells NE
< BaseChanger that it should not assume a complete circular sequence, allowing the entry of a much sho
< rter sequence.  However, partial sequences will need to include sufficient sequence flanking the mut
< ation site, currently set at a minimum of 35 nt 5\u2032 and 25 nt 3\u2032. Mutations will be prohibi
< ted from being too close to the ends of the provided partial sequence fragment and cannot span the e
< nds of the fragment.',P=S(),G=c("a"),G.textContent="\u2191 Back to top",O=S(),K=c("h3"),K.textConten
< t="APPLICATION MODES",D=S(),L=c("h4"),L.textContent="Point Mutation Mode",R=S(),Q=c("p"),Q.textConte
< nt=`AA Point Mutation mode is intended to facilitate the specification of one or more point mutation
< s (single codon changes). 	This mode only supports sequence replacements of exactly 3 bases (1 
< codon), and it does not support deletions or insertions.	Multiple single point mutations can 
< be entered at one time. A Merge mutations option is also available to combine adjacent point mutatio
< ns in a single primer. If multiple point mutations are specified, the "Generate primers for NEBuilde
< r HiFi" option is posible, where NEBaseChanger will generate primer pairs compatible with the NEBuil
< der HiFi DNA Assembly Master Mix to simplify the execution of multiple	site-directed mutagenesis in
<  a single reaction. The option is only displayed when multiple mutations are specified in point muta
< tion mode.`,ae=S(),W=c("p"),W.textContent="First, enter the start position of the ORF, either direct
< ly by entering the coordinate or by clicking in the DNA sequence row of the codon view. Setting the 
< ORF start position will highlight the ORF. ORF start position must be a whole number within the sequ
< ence; an invalid value shows a warning instead of building primers. Use the Next and Prev buttons to
<  locate and highlight the next or previous ORF. Changing the ORF start keeps the mutations you've en
< tered; any whose amino acid no longer matches the new reading frame is skipped, with a warning, unti
< l you edit it or move the ORF start back.",x=S(),H=c("p"),H.textContent=`Next, enter one or more mut
< ations of the form [old AA][codon #][new AA],	for example, M2A, F32H, C45Y, etc., separated by spa
< ces, commas or semicolons. The codon # is relative to the selected 	ORF start.  Optionally, spec
< ify the exact triplet replacement by appending 	a colon followed by the triplet, for example, M2G:GG
< G, A34F:TTC. Exact triplets, 	will override automatic selection.`,U=S(),le=c("p"),le.textContent=`
< Clicking on an amino acid in the codon view will initiate a dialog to select the replacement	amin
< o acid, including the exact triplet, and will add it to the list of mutations.	The old AA identity 
< is checked, but processing is not halted if the old AA does not match	the indicated codon #. The c
< odon number takes presidence.`,J=S(),ie=c("p"),ie.innerHTML="Select a codon selection strategy, eith
< er maximum codon usage or maximum parsimony.  For the former, codon usage is obtained from <i>E. col
< i K12</i>. For maximum parsimony, a simple sequence distance is calculated as the required number of
<  base changes to go from the original codon to the replacement codon, and the triplet is chosen to m
< inimize the changes.",z=S(),te=c("p"),te.textContent=`Normally, for substitutions like AA point muta
< tions, where the target region encompasses just 3 nucleotides, the replacement sequence 	will
<  be placed in the forward primer with 10 or more bases of annealing sequence flanking the inserted b
< ases. If the "Confine mutations to primer 5\u2032 tails" option is selected, the replacement sequenc
< e will always be attached to the 5\u2032 end of the primers. The "5\u2032 tails" option is incompati
< ble with NEBuilder HiFi primer option (see below).`,pe=S(),Y=c("p"),Y.textContent=`If multiple mutat
< ions are entered and cluster together closely (ideally adjacent), the "merge mutations" option can b
< e selected. This option combines point mutations to keep them within a single primer pair, when poss
< ible. Mutations are entered normally in the form [old AA][codon #][new AA]:[triplet], 	for example,
<  M1A, D3H, C4F:TTT, etc., separated by spaces, commas or semicolons.	If the mutations are close t
< ogether, generally not separated by more than 6 bases, 	the mutations are merged and treated as a si
< ngle sequence replacement operation. 	In the example above, all 3 mutations would be embedded in a
<  single primer pair.	This option is currently only compatible with mutations confined to the 5\u2
< 032 primer tail.`,ue=S(),he=c("p"),he.innerHTML=`If the &quot;Generate primers for NEBuilder HiFi&qu
< ot; option is selected, NEBaseChanger will generate primer pairs compatible with	the NEBuilde
< r HiFi DNA Assembly Master Mix to simplify the execution of multiple	site-directed mutagenesis in
<  a single reaction. 	NEBuilder HiFi primers cannot be generated if mutations are confined to the 
< 5<sup>\u2032</sup> tails, and the option will not be displayed, nor is it compatible with merged mut
< ations. Individual mutations need to be sufficiently spaced apart	to avoid overlap clashes bet
< ween adjacent forward and reverse primers.`,de=S(),_e=c("p"),_e.innerHTML='Details on using NEBuilde
< r HiFi for multiple site mutations are available <a href="https://www.neb.com/-/media/nebus/files/ap
< plication-notes/appnote_improved_methods_for_sdm_using_nebuilder_hifi_dna_assembly_master_mix.pdf?re
< v=918a4c52177641cbb8e2087a1286b9f4" target="_blank">here</a>.',ne=S(),$=c("h4"),$.textContent="Indel
< /Substitution Mutation Mode",fe=S(),we=c("p"),we.textContent=`Indel/Substitution mode is a general m
< ode that facilitates the specification of mutations of arbitrary length on the input sequence.	Subs
< titution and insertion sequences of up to 100 bp are allowed.`,j=c("p"),j.innerHTML=`Insert/delete/s
< ubstitute (indel) operations require a 5&#39; flanking position (start), a  	3&#39; flanking posi
< tion (end), and a replacement sequence. The target sequence to be   	replaced is <b>between</b> t
< he start and end positions. First, enter the start and end coordinates.  	Optionally, click an
< d drag (text select) over the target sequence in either of the DNA sequence rows.  	The target a
< nd flanking bases will be highlighted and the start/end coordinates filled in.  	For insertio
< ns, clicking between two bases will select the proper flanking bases.`,F=S(),ee=c("p"),ee.textConten
< t=`To delete a sequence, leave the replacement sequence blank.  	To insert a sequence, the st
< art and end should be consecutive positions.   	The replacement sequence will be inserted between th
< em.`,V=S(),me=c("p"),me.innerHTML=`For example, if start/end is 234/239 and the replacement sequence
<  is ACGT,   	the operation will substitute the sequence between bases 234 and 239 with ACGT.  
< 	This release of NEBaseChanger will design primers   	accommodating inserts up to a maximu
< m of <strong>100</strong> nucleotides.  	Note that multiple mutations can be included within 
< a single  	replacement sequence as long as the sequence uses only non-ambiguous base codes. For
<  example,   	if two amino acids need to be changed using a single primer pair, the start/end is  
< 	set to flank the targeted codons, and the replacement sequence (designed manually) contains 
<   	the required substitutions at each codon.`,_t=S(),Je=c("p"),Je.textContent=`Ambiguous base c
< odes can be entered in the replacement sequence (N,Y,S,W, etc)   	and will be expanded combina
< torialy over multiple primers.   	For example, a replacement sequence containing NS will be ex
< panded to 8 sequences   	containing: AC, CC, GC, TC, AG, CG, GG, and TG, generating 8 primer 
< pairs.`,bt=S(),ut=c("p"),ut.textContent='If the "Confine mutations to primer 5\u2032 tails" option i
< s selected, the replacement sequence will always be attached to the 5\u2032 end of the primers, rega
< rdless of the length of the substitution. This option is incompatible with NEBuilder HiFi primer opt
< ion (see below).',it=S(),Be=c("p"),Be.textContent=`Normally, for substitutions, if the target region
<  is longer than 6 nucleotides, 	the substitution sequence will be split between the two primers, att
< ached 	to the 5\u2032 end of the primers as non-annealing tails. The 5\u2032 ends 	of the annea
< ling portions of the primers align with the edges of the target region. 	If the target region
<  encompasses 6 or fewer nucleotides, the replacement sequence 	will be placed in the forward primer
<  with 10 or more bases of annealing sequence 	flanking the inserted bases.`,We=S(),Ie=c("a"),Ie.te
